  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Heat 2 tbsp oil in a large skillet over high heat. Cook the peppers and onion with the chili powder, cumin and a pinch of salt, stirring now and then, until charred and soft, 8 to 10 minutes. Move to a plate.",
      "uses": ["oil", "pepper", "onion", "chili", "cumin", "salt"],
      "timerMinutes": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the rest of the oil and the cauliflower rice to the pan. Cook until tender and any liquid has evaporated, about 5 minutes. Stir in the juice of 1 lime, the cilantro and a pinch of salt.",
      "uses": ["cauli", "lime", "cilantro"],
      "timerMinutes": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "Divide the cauliflower rice between bowls and top with the fajita vegetables, avocado and salsa. Serve with lime wedges.",
